// Molly's provenance unit test "aggregate rewrites don't affect grouping by including un-aggregated variables" (a
// regression test; R06 §12.6, ProvenanceSuite): a and b each send a vote to M at time 1; vote_cnt(M, count<I>) groups
// by M only, although the body also binds V, so vote_cnt(M, 2) holds from time 2 with two contributors, and each
// vote's loss falsifies it. The program is the unit test's with a pre/post pair added. Blossom golden corpus,
// transcribed from R06 (derived = true); see ../../README.md.

vote(M, V)@next :- vote(M, V);
member(M, V, I)@next :- member(M, V, I);
vote(M, V)@async :- begin(V, M);

vote_cnt(M, count<I>) :- vote(M, V), member(M, V, I);
good(M, I) :- vote_cnt(M, I);

// pre: M's members; post: the member, provided both votes are counted in one group (vote_cnt(M, 2))
pre(M, I) :- member(M, V, I);
post(M, I) :- vote_cnt(M, N), member(M, V, I), N == 2;

member("M", "a", 1)@1;
member("M", "b", 2)@1;
begin("a", "M")@1;
begin("b", "M")@1;
